   "issue": "`minkowskiProduct_add_self_of_realPhoton_energyFraction` and `energyFraction_eq_exp_rapidity_mul` (line 199) bind `\u03b3 : PhotonKinematics` only through `\u03b3.energy`, while `hq`/`hq'` force `\u27eaq,q\u27eb\u2098 = 0`. Nothing constrains `\u03b3.virtuality`, so both can be instantiated with a `\u03b3` whose record says `Q\u00b2 \u2260 0`; the docstrings say \"a real photon\" and the conclusions drop the `q\u00b2` term that `minkowskiProduct_add_self_of_target` keeps explicit. This is the trap of roadmap convention 1 (\"photon virtuality is explicit data, never a default\"), and it bites in-repo: `ChargedSource.virtuality_pos_of_mem_photonRegion` (Basic.lean:321) proves every photon of a massive source's `photonRegion` has `0 < k.virtuality`, i.e. exactly the photons a downstream flux statement would feed to these lemmas can never satisfy the lightlike `q` assumed here.",
